{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-17480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=5,$ and the sum of the first $11$ terms is ${S}_{11}=374?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-17480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=11$, $d=5$, and ${S}_{N}=374$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}374 & =\\frac{11}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(11-1)(5)) \\\\ 748 & =11(2{a}_{1}+50) \\\\ 68 & =2{a}_{1}+50 \\\\ 18 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-17480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "03d298192812bd318a5933b8129432354b379a88ce49cc13a32b6c19c3adb862"} {"question" "q-17480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-17480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-17480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-76376" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the first term of an arithmetic series if its $17$th term is $33$ and the sum of the first $30$ terms is $1\\,080.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-76376" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=30$ and ${S}_{N}=1\\,080$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 1\\,080 & =\\frac{30}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(30-1)d) \\\\ 1\\,080 & =15(2{a}_{1}+29d) \\\\ \\frac{1\\,080}{15} & =2{a}_{1}+29d \\\\ 72 & =2{a}_{1}+29d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $17$th term of the arithmetic series  and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{17} & ={a}_{1}+(17-1)d \\\\ 33 & ={a}_{1}+16d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}33={a}_{1}+16d \\\\ 72=2{a}_{1}+29d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-66 & =-2{a}_{1}-32d \\\\ 72 & =2{a}_{1}+29d \\\\ 6 & =-3d \\\\ d & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}33 & ={a}_{1}+16(-2) \\\\ 33 & ={a}_{1}-32 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =65.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-76376" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "03d298192812bd318a5933b8129432354b379a88ce49cc13a32b6c19c3adb862"} {"question" "q-76376" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-76376" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-68"] ["math" "-77"] ["math" "62"] ["math" "65"] ["math" "71"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-76376" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "65"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-108635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=0.6,$ and the sum of the first $37$ terms is ${S}_{37}=444?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-108635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=37$, $d=0.6$, and ${S}_{N}=444$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}444 & =\\frac{37}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(37-1)(0.6)) \\\\ 888 & =37(2{a}_{1}+21.6) \\\\ \\frac{888}{37} & =2{a}_{1}+21.6 \\\\ 2.4 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-108635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "03d298192812bd318a5933b8129432354b379a88ce49cc13a32b6c19c3adb862"} {"question" "q-108635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-108635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.2"] ["math" "1.5"] ["math" "1.9"] ["math" "2.6"] ["math" "2.9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-108635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-108637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=\\frac{5}{7},$ and the sum of the first $50$ terms is ${S}_{50}=1\\,125?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-108637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=50$, $d=\\frac{5}{7}$, and ${S}_{N}=1\\,125$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\,125 & =\\frac{50}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(50-1)(\\frac{5}{7})) \\\\ 1\\,125 & =25(2{a}_{1}+35) \\\\ 45 & =2{a}_{1}+35 \\\\ 10 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-108637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "03d298192812bd318a5933b8129432354b379a88ce49cc13a32b6c19c3adb862"} {"question" "q-108637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-108637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-108637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-250865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the $10$th term of an arithmetic series is $-\\frac{1}{5}$ and the sum of the first $21$ terms is $0,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-250865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=21$ and ${S}_{N}=0$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{21}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(21-1)d) \\\\ 0 & =21(2{a}_{1}+20d) \\\\ 0 & =2{a}_{1}+20d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $10$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{10} & ={a}_{1}+(10-1)d \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+9d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} & \\,\\,\\,=\\,{a}_{1}+9d \\\\ \\,0 & \\,\\,\\,=\\,2{a}_{1}+20d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & =-2{a}_{1}-18d \\\\ 0 & =2{a}_{1}+20d \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =2d \\\\ d & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=\\frac{1}{5}$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+9d \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+9(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{9}{5} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-250865" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "03d298192812bd318a5933b8129432354b379a88ce49cc13a32b6c19c3adb862"} {"question" "q-250865" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"} {"question" "q-250865" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063615/state.json" "file_sha256" "e6c3effa1b1724ed3c6e0ffe691c5d0fad608b73fc9a0ec163ed0ca63dac68a0"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2062 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
